# Provider binaries and the working directory.
.terraform/

# State, and the backups Terraform writes beside it. It holds the database
# password in the clear — that is what state is, not a bug — so it never goes
# near the repository.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Real values, including whatever a private deployment calls itself.
*.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Saved plans, which hold the same secrets state does.
*.tfplan

crash.log
crash.*.log

# Note what is NOT here: .terraform.lock.hcl is committed. It pins the provider
# versions and their checksums, which is the difference between CI validating
# what you validated and CI validating something else.
